Preparing later F009 cohorts
===========================

Purpose and review gate
-----------------------

This package supplies new metadata Source for cohorts after the presently
owned interval 330..341.  It does not initialize a cohort, register a cache
entry, alter progress, launch a worker, or evaluate an Original forest
during preparation.  Its packet has Root authority false.  The three
operational entries must not execute before a distinct Source peer and
Root's complete Source/protocol ownership.  A future init additionally
requires the exact expected registered prefix, at least 342.  It therefore
cannot freeze the next cohort while the present cohort remains unregistered.

The reviewer interface is explicit.  A positive Source peer must have
status beginning SUPPORTED_STATIC, empty blockers, reviewer different from
/root and this package's author, and exact fields ``programs`` (mapping
entry filenames to whole descriptors), ``entry_manifests`` (the packet's
complete mapping), ``packet`` and ``protocol``.  These pin the complete
current Source rather than inheriting a lost review or old file name.
Root alone subsequently runs an entry with --actor /root, by a genuine
Root API issue.  The argument is a role declaration; later actual review
must establish the caller and genuine API/guard records.

