Paths and reproduction
-----------------------

New operational Source and all retained bodies are durable under this
directory.  ``legacy_inputs.json`` maps every consumed original descriptor
and schema example to a content-addressed retained object.  For a clean
reproduction, restore these byte-identical legacy aliases to their exact
listed paths before Root issues any entry.  Existing files must match the
listed complete sizes and SHA256; an unmatched existing file must not be
overwritten.  This is restoration of genuine retained bytes, not creation
of a substitute historical artifact.  Source peer and Root review must
cover whichever restoration mechanism is used.  The new entries themselves
refuse missing or mismatched inputs and do not restore them implicitly.

The public repository layout or its restore procedure must preserve this
mapping and all objects; none of the new reproducible inputs is supplied
