role stems and Root SDK keys are unchanged.  These Sources create no
scientific directory and schedule no worker.

Initialization
---------------

After registration of the current cohort and synchronization of current
intake, controller and runtime, Root may issue init_cohort.py with
--actor /root, --expected-prefix N and --Source-peer PATH BYTES SHA256.
The entry checks N equals both registered-prefix counters, checks the
strict-slot counter and adopted R4 roster, and checks the controller's
checkpoint is the current-intake checkpoint.  It also reconciles L026's
paid count with its accepted receipt.  All three exact progress editions
are then frozen into the new cohort.

Runtime cache values and bank cache values are never JSON-decoded.
Lexical projection reads only typed counts, cache-key names and bank
descriptors.  Keys must be disjoint across banks, and each prospective
parent-pair key must be absent.  The entry checks the old individual
scientific paths and the new cohort science/control directories are fresh.
The new interval has at most twelve parents, partitioned into at most
four consecutive batches of one to three.  The init emits only a new
Source owner and cohort, with empty metadata subdirectories.  It writes
no canonical file and issues no scientific role.

The cohort keeps ROOT_F009_CONTIGUOUS_PARENT_COHORT_V1 and the old active
adapter program/handoff/peer descriptors.  Its extra preparation_provenance
pins this new package, init Source, current manifest, peer and protocol.
The V2 Source owner explicitly owns the current metadata Source/disclosures
and the unchanged old scientific meanings.  It does not claim to have
read any missing old bookkeeping.  Each later entry checks the new owner,
cohort/package identity and exact frozen progress editions.

Phase preparation
------------------

Root issues issue_phase.py with --actor /root, --cohort PATH BYTES SHA,
--batch B, --phase prepare_suppliers|assemble_strict|close_pairing, and
--Source-peer PATH BYTES SHA.  The decision, bindings and metadata guard
for that batch/phase must be fresh.  The first phase requires a fresh
scientific batch base.  Later phases require the immediately preceding
prepared metadata, correct cohort/batch/indices and an absent later output.
The parent and certificate payloads in strict_preparation are lexically
skipped.  Only successful first-v1 scientific SDKs are bound automatically,
with original 128 MiB/150-second invocation caps.  The unchanged adapter
will perform its existing exact guard/result/request/certificate joins.

The fresh decision preserves ROOT_F009_COHORT_BATCH_PHASE_DECISION_V1,
the old adapter's independent peer and all existing Root duties.  It also
records metadata_decision_issuer and metadata_decision_issuer_Source_peer
for this new entry, plus its current preparation packet/manifest.  The
binding schema stays ROOT_F009_COHORT_ROLE_ACTUAL_BINDINGS_V1.  The entry
prints the exact old-adapter argv under the unchanged 256 MiB/125-second
metadata supervisor.  It never executes that argv.  Root separately owns
each actual metadata phase and each actual scientific role.

No successful phase ownership is reissued.  A genuinely refused metadata
attempt may use a separately owned exact-argv retry and attempt map; a
successful attempt must never be rerun for logging or certificate shape.
The unchanged adapter's broader explicit scientific retry ABI is not
automated by this successor.  A scientific pre-entry refusal requires a
separately reviewed binding/closer/auditor extension; it does not authorize
replaying a successful scientific role.

Closing and independent actual review
-------------------------------------

Root issues close_cohort.py with the same actor/cohort/Source-peer inputs.
An optional --attempts PATH BYTES SHA selects an explicitly Root-owned
ROOT_F009_COHORT_METADATA_PHASE_ATTEMPTS_V1 map.  Without that argument the
entry creates a fresh map with zero overrides.  Zero through three times
the number of batches are allowed.  Each override selects edition 2..8,
lists every earlier non-success SDK, retains genuine Root API returns,
requires the same exact argv and the existing pre-entry-refusal message.
No successful attempt can appear in a refusal history.

The closer reads only typed cohort/pairing counts, source indices and
terminal scientific/metadata SDK metadata.  Pairing forest values remain
opaque.  Every science role is terminal first-v1.  The summary preserves
ROOT_F009_COMPLETED_COHORT_ACTUAL_SUMMARY_V1 and its fields; all_roles_terminal_first_v1
is true exactly when the metadata override map is empty.  It separately
reports Source and business reads, a helper preload, and a conservative
entry/common Source bootstrap allowance.  It writes only an optional
fresh zero-override map and fresh summary.  Registration remains false,
whole-R5/census credit remains false and independent actual review remains
pending.  No numerical Source is imported.

The separate generic actual auditor is owned by /root/forest_resume.
Its config must pin this new phase issuer/peer for a future cohort, and
this new closer/peer where its interface requires them.  It tolerates
preparation_provenance while retaining the same cohort, phase, SDK and
role paths.  Its currently reviewed ownership admission is for the exact
old V1 owner of cohort 330.  Admission of the honest new V2 owner requires
a separately reviewed successor branch; that branch is not implemented
or claimed accepted by this package.  It is a required integration step
before a future cohort can pass actual review or be adopted.  That audit
and Root's later registration are separate from this package.  No current
cohort or future cohort is adopted here.

Bounds and outputs
-------------------

Every entry requires Python -E -B -S without optimization, a 125-second
alarm, cooperative 115-second completion and a 256 MiB RSS limit.
The literal metadata Ledger requires at most 4 MiB per file, 64 MiB
cumulative reads and 512 paths.  Complete initial and closing reads,
all current entry/common/helper Source, protocol/peer/manifest inputs,
nominal project Source bootstrap and output verification share that
envelope.  Planned outputs are bounded, exclusive and read back; fresh
directories are created only after closing input checks.  Every active
entry plus literal common/helper, inherited guard bodies and 512 reserve
is below 65536 bytes, as recorded by its manifest.

A runtime or bank exceeding the per-file limit is refused.  There is no
silent larger read, partial-file hash, changed scientific cap or fallback
Original evaluation.  Root must then use a separately reviewed metadata
banking operation.  The package records a plan and Source only; no
operational entry, worker, numerical control or future snapshot has been
executed to prepare it.
